WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:02.601
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Chelsea Handler.

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:04.003
We were talking backstage.

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:06.239
Obviously, you have a history
as being a talk-show host.

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:08.508
But this summer, you filled in
for a full week,

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:09.542
for Jimmy Kimmell.

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:11.044
-Mm.
-Did a great job. How was it?

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:13.512
Did you find it took you awhile
to get your host legs back

00:00:13.512 --> 00:00:14.847
or was it immediate?

00:00:14.847 --> 00:00:16.749
-No. It was right after
Roe v. Wade was overturned,

00:00:16.749 --> 00:00:17.883
so I was ready to rumble.

00:00:17.883 --> 00:00:19.085
I mean, the timing--
[ Audience laughs ]

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:20.886
The timing couldn't have been
any more perfect.

00:00:20.886 --> 00:00:23.689
And I have to say, like,
I didn't miss doing that

00:00:23.689 --> 00:00:25.692
until I did it again,
and then, I remembered.

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:28.060
I was like, "Oh, this is exactly
what I'm built for."

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:30.729
You know, just kind of,
like, real commentary.

00:00:30.729 --> 00:00:32.932
You know, about being able
to comment on things

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:36.068
in real-time on a platform
is a great, you know,

00:00:36.068 --> 00:00:38.204
advantage to have
and it's a great --

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:40.406
It's something we're definitely
missing for --

00:00:40.406 --> 00:00:42.241
You know, there is a dirth
of women doing this,

00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:44.144
and it's not cool anymore.

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:45.778
So I'm definitely going to get
back in the mix.

00:00:45.778 --> 00:00:46.913
-That's great.
-And do it again, yeah.

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:48.314
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:50.483
-I always say, and I'm sure
you feel the same way,

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:52.718
like, is that having
a platform saves me

00:00:52.718 --> 00:00:54.754
from just muttering
to myself in the street.

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:56.055
Like, you have, obviously,

00:00:56.055 --> 00:00:57.589
standup saves you
in the same way.

00:00:57.589 --> 00:00:58.724
But I know what you mean.

00:00:58.724 --> 00:01:00.593
Like, I would imagine
that you step away

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:01.727
and you have more time,
and that's great.

00:01:01.727 --> 00:01:03.363
But you get it back
and it must just be like

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:05.031
right into your veins
how much fun it is.

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:06.666
-Absolutely, and it's also,
it's like, you know --

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:08.634
You guys are all great
and woke and liberal

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:09.902
and you're all for
women's rights.

00:01:09.902 --> 00:01:12.438
But we need women up there,
like, standing up for us

00:01:12.438 --> 00:01:14.407
commenting on this.

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:15.642
You know, we like --

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:18.411
It's just, it's crazy
in this day and age

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:21.647
that we don't have more females
on TV doing the same thing.

00:01:21.647 --> 00:01:24.317
So, it just needs to happen,
so I'm gonna make it happen.

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:25.485
Alright, well,
you're the perfect person

00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:26.586
to make it happen.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:29.188
I know, you did
"Chelsea Lately" forever,

00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:30.790
but if you did it again

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.458
you would have
a different name for it.

00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:33.993
-Well, "Chelsea Later" maybe.

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:35.161
[ Audience laughs ]

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:37.329
"Chelsea Later Much", yeah.
-[ Chuckles ]

00:01:37.329 --> 00:01:39.031
You what the other
thing is that I think is --

00:01:39.031 --> 00:01:41.033
You know, everyone complains.
Not everybody complains.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:42.502
But there's a group
of people that complain about

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:44.504
the political correctness
that we live in right now.

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:46.672
And, I find that to be annoying.

00:01:46.672 --> 00:01:49.442
Because as a comedian,
it is your job to be clever

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:50.843
and to think outside the box.

00:01:50.843 --> 00:01:53.045
And if somebody puts up
parameters in saying,

00:01:53.045 --> 00:01:55.281
" You can't be sexist,
and you can't be racist."

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:57.183
That's not a tall order.
-No.

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:59.251
You know, so, like,
I would like to take

00:01:59.251 --> 00:02:01.587
all the comics from
"Chelsea Lately," those days,

00:02:01.587 --> 00:02:05.291
Fortune Feimster, you know,
Tiffany Haddish, Jo Koy,

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:07.793
and all the you comics
that are coming up now,

00:02:07.793 --> 00:02:09.395
and put them together
on a roundtable

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:12.765
to comment on what's going on in
our current political,

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:14.500
you know, and cultural
and social

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:15.835
and everything that's happening,

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:18.103
and show people how easy
it is to be funny

00:02:18.103 --> 00:02:19.638
without being sexist or racist.

00:02:19.638 --> 00:02:20.706
-And I think the other thing...

00:02:20.706 --> 00:02:21.708
[ Audience cheers ]

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:22.841
...is you can --

00:02:22.841 --> 00:02:24.143
You know, I always kind of say,

00:02:24.143 --> 00:02:26.112
"Oh, you can still be sexist
and racist, just then,

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:28.380
people are allowed to say
'You're a sexist and a racist.'"

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:29.549
-Yeah.
-It's like, that's the part

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:31.350
is it's this weird thing
that it's always like,

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:34.120
"No, I deserve diplomatic
immunity to do whatever I want."

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:37.023
-Yeah, and I like the challenge
of parameters because if you

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:39.091
left me to my own devices,
you know,

00:02:39.091 --> 00:02:41.127
I mean, I would be
in a gutter somewhere.

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:43.162
-Yeah. We all know that.

00:02:43.162 --> 00:02:44.997
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.997 --> 00:02:48.400
-Thanks. Thank you. Thank you.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:49.836
-You have a hosting gig
coming up.

00:02:49.836 --> 00:02:51.804
You're hosting
the Critics Choice Awards

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:54.073
after the holidays.
Do you approach that --

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:56.809
So, that's a room that will be
full of peers of yours,

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:58.844
people who did great work
over the course of the year.

00:02:58.844 --> 00:03:01.380
Do you approach it differently
than you do a normal gig?

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:03.917
-No. I mean, I think I'm just
there to keep the show

00:03:03.917 --> 00:03:06.119
moving along,
high energy and funny.

00:03:06.119 --> 00:03:09.255
I mean, I'm not going to, like,
go in on anybody unless --

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:11.357
well, unless there's
a really big target.

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:13.959
[ Laughter ]
But I mean, it's just more --

00:03:13.959 --> 00:03:16.496
-Should somebody be worried
if like a cobbler comes over

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:19.565
to their table, like right
before your monologue?

00:03:19.565 --> 00:03:21.601
-You mean a shoe cobbler
or a blackberry cobbler?

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:23.703
-Your blackberry cobbler, yeah.
-Yeah, no.

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:25.204
Well, he's open season.

00:03:25.204 --> 00:03:26.872
Woody Allen you're allowed to
make fun of.

00:03:26.872 --> 00:03:28.308
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Yeah, no.

00:03:28.308 --> 00:03:29.509
Nobody should be really worried.

00:03:29.509 --> 00:03:31.710
I just want to make it
fun and light.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:34.179
Those award ceremonies
can go on and on for hours,

00:03:34.179 --> 00:03:36.015
and they can be so boring.

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:37.884
-Yeah. When you host them,
you have to do --

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:39.552
you front-load what
you want to say

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:41.020
because over the course of
the night, they're just

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:43.689
less and less happy to see you.
-Yes, that's right. Exactly.

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:45.791
-You are between them and the
after-party at that point.

00:03:45.791 --> 00:03:47.693
-I'm going to have to get
a second outfit change

00:03:47.693 --> 00:03:49.194
that is going to rev things up.

00:03:49.194 --> 00:03:50.630
-Okay, that's very smart.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:53.098
We know at the very least, we
have a better outfit coming.

00:03:53.098 --> 00:03:55.401
-Especially and you know how shy
I am with my body.

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:57.670
-Yes. You're finally coming
out of your shell.

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:59.238
We're very happy about it.
-I'm ready to show off

00:03:59.238 --> 00:04:00.873
everything that I've gotten.

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:04.243
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.243 --> 00:04:05.611
-Will you be skiing
this holiday?

00:04:05.611 --> 00:04:08.314
-Speaking of topless,

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:10.483
will you be skiing during
this holiday season?

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:12.017
[ Laughter ]
I do, you guys.

00:04:12.017 --> 00:04:14.987
I make a topless video every ski
season for my birthday

00:04:14.987 --> 00:04:17.122
because --
with a margarita and a joint

00:04:17.122 --> 00:04:18.624
because those are
two of my passions.

00:04:18.624 --> 00:04:22.294
-Yeah. If there was
a Chelsea Handler state flag,

00:04:22.294 --> 00:04:25.331
it would be those two things.
-It would be that, and then it

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:28.200
would be boobs because I love to
share my boobs with everybody.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.736
I was so embarrassed of my big
boobs when I was a little girl.

00:04:30.736 --> 00:04:34.574
Then I finally grew into them,
and now I love 'em, you know?

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:36.175
I can't get enough of them.

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:37.810
And I just want to share them
with the world

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:40.680
and body positivity
and, yeah, look at 'em go.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.215
[ Laughter ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:44.049
-Well, happy holidays
to all of us.

00:04:44.049 --> 00:04:47.152
-Happy holidays to
the whole wide world.

00:04:47.152 --> 00:04:49.121
-Hey, thank you so much
for being here.

00:04:49.121 --> 00:04:51.124
I cannot wait to see
this special.

00:04:51.124 --> 00:04:52.625
It's always such a pleasure
to have you here.

00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:54.093
-Thank you so much, Seth.
Thank you.

00:04:54.093 --> 00:04:55.461
-Chelsea Handler, everybody.

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:56.895
Her new special "Revolution"

00:04:56.895 --> 00:04:58.698
premieres on Netflix
December 27th.

00:04:58.698 --> 00:05:00.700
We'll be right back
with Martin McDonagh.

